# Reforge Bench

## Product

A hardware and firmware workbench with a shared machine/instrument state contract.
User data and analysis providers are separate from the state model.

## Architecture

| Component | Role |
| --- | --- |
| BenchSnapshot | Shared machine/instrument state contract |
| MachineState | Known or unavailable machine measurements |
| InstrumentState | Device sample identity and freshness |
| Diagnostics | Bounded private records and metadata-only reports |
| DiagnosticEvent / Failure | Typed local failure context, not directly serializable |
| DiagnosticReport | Typed, serializable allowlisted metadata |
| Command | Typed, local read-only CLI actions |

## Contract

- Source provenance is simulated, recorded or producer-declared live.
- Missing numeric measurements are null, not zero.
- Numeric measurements must be finite; spindle speed must be non-negative.
- Snapshot validation does not authenticate transport or qualify measurements.

## Example

The curated hardware/REA case under crates/bench-cli/examples/hardware-rea/ contains
selected factual observations and recorded aggregate measurements, not synthetic
signals or raw firmware/captures. Its provenance is recorded_summary, not live.
It requires no device access or external tool installation to read.

## Verification

The Rust tests cover snapshot validity, diagnostic bounds/deduplication and
private-text exclusion from shared reports. The graph does not prove runtime or
hardware coverage.
